sc-1-p3 = prose (cons "Consider a byte buffer \(b\), its length \(s\), and an output record \(o\). The source operation decodes a four-byte header consisting of a 16-bit tag and 16-bit payload length, followed by a borrowed payload slice. The result is failure when \(s<4\) or when the payload length exceeds \(s-4\). Otherwise it writes \(\mathsf{tag},\mathsf{len},\mathsf{ptr}\) into the output record and returns success. **Header reads are defined only after the length guard succeeds**; the source semantics must not perform an out-of-bounds read merely to decide whether a short input is valid. Write \(b\) for the readable buffer and \(\mu\) for the initial memory." nil)
